cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this formalization, please cite it as below, together with the
  preprint it formalizes. S. Armstrong was supported by the European Research
  Council (ERC) under the European Union's Horizon Europe research and
  innovation programme, grant agreement number 101200828. S. Serfaty was
  supported by a Simons Investigator award, NSF grant DMS-2247846, and the
  Institut Universitaire de France.
title: "TriangularMinimality: a Lean 4 formalization of triangular minimality for the planar Coulomb renormalized energy"
version: "1.0"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of the OpenAI preprint
  "Triangular minimality for planar Coulomb renormalized energy" and of the
  corresponding lower bound for the jellium energy of Chapter 11 of S.
  Serfaty's "Lectures on Coulomb and Riesz gases". It proves that the
  triangular lattice of covolume one minimizes the planar Coulomb renormalized
  energy among admissible fields (Theorem 1.1), the lower bound for n points
  on a square torus from which this follows (Theorem 1.2), and the resulting
  value of the second term of the minimal logarithmic energy of n points on the
  sphere (Corollary 1.3). The finite interval computation of the preprint is
  replaced by a certificate checked by the Lean kernel. The proofs use only the
  standard axioms.
